# cross-lib-activity — Lib A (the referring policy library).
library "Root".

// Root's decision recommends the sibling Shared library's activity via the
// cross-library qualified ref `"Shared"."Shared Deny"` — with NO explicit
// `include "Shared"`. The cross-lib `recommend activity` alone must pull Shared
// into BOTH the CQL emit closure (`cqlByLibrary`) AND the FHIR emit closure
// (#196 / this fix). Pre-#196 the FHIR activityResolver returned null for any
// qualified cross-library activity ref, so this surfaced directly as an
// `unresolved-activity` UnmatchedReference, which then cascaded the decision to
// `decision-cascade-suppressed`. It now resolves to Shared's Recommendation
// PlanDefinition, and the CQL-closure fix emits Shared's CQL so its FHIR Library
// no longer dangles at Inv 4 — WITHOUT the author needing a `redundant-local-include`.

concept "Active Crohns Disease":
- type is Condition.
- value type is boolean.
- code is `active-crohns-disease`.
- definition is exists this.

decision "Triage Crohns":
- when "Active Crohns Disease" then recommend activity "Shared"."Shared Deny".
